[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Constitutional AI and Rule Overrides (Part 1 of 3)","textKn":"ಸಂವಿಧಾನಾತ್ಮಕ AI ಮತ್ತು ನಿಯಮ ಅತಿಕ್ರಮಣಗಳು (ಭಾಗ 1 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 1 of 3: enumerated rules against a labelled set, the four-tier priority resolver with a hard-prohibition check first, an operator allowlist against a naive merge, a mislabelled category and six unit tests that are run. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of the ideas behind constitutional AI and rule overrides (enumerated rules against principles, a four-tier priority resolver, hard prohibitions, an operator allowlist, unknown evaluations, critique-and-revise and preference data flow, authority of document text, a policy gate with approval binding, policy integrity and drift metrics), not the real software, and the evaluations, the critique table, the scores, the labelled set and the model versions are all written by the lab author as scripts, no model is trained or queried, the tools are simulated and nothing is executed, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The original code/main.py was not supplied and the lesson code was shown only in fragments, so the labs are our own implementation and the outputs were produced by running them. The lesson description of the 2022 Constitutional AI method, RLAIF, the 2023 participatory experiment and the 2026 Claude Constitution is conceptual or cited and was not run or checked here, and the labs involve no model. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 1ನೆಯದು: ಲೇಬಲ್ ಮಾಡಿದ ಸೆಟ್ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಪಟ್ಟಿ ಮಾಡಿದ ನಿಯಮಗಳು, ಮೊದಲು ಕಠಿಣ-ನಿಷೇಧ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ ಇರುವ ನಾಲ್ಕು-ಹಂತದ ಆದ್ಯತೆ resolver, ನೈವ್ ವಿಲೀನದ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಆಪರೇಟರ್ allowlist, ತಪ್ಪಾಗಿ ಲೇಬಲ್ ಮಾಡಿದ ವರ್ಗ ಮತ್ತು ಓಡಿಸಿದ ಆರು unit ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆಗಳು. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು ಸಂವಿಧಾನಾತ್ಮಕ AI ಮತ್ತು ನಿಯಮ ಅತಿಕ್ರಮಣಗಳು (ಪಟ್ಟಿ ಮಾಡಿದ ನಿಯಮಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ತತ್ವಗಳು, ನಾಲ್ಕು-ಹಂತದ ಆದ್ಯತೆ resolver, ಕಠಿಣ ನಿಷೇಧಗಳು, ಆಪರೇಟರ್ allowlist, ಅಜ್ಞಾತ ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನಗಳು, critique-and-revise ಮತ್ತು ಆದ್ಯತೆ ದತ್ತಾಂಶ ಹರಿವು, ದಾಖಲೆ ಪಠ್ಯದ ಅಧಿಕಾರ, ಅನುಮೋದನೆ ಬಂಧ ಇರುವ ನೀತಿ gate, ನೀತಿ ಸಮಗ್ರತೆ ಮತ್ತು drift ಮಾಪನಗಳು) ಹಿಂದಿನ ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, ನಿಜವಾದ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನಗಳು, critique ಟೇಬಲ್, ಅಂಕಗಳು, ಲೇಬಲ್ ಮಾಡಿದ ಸೆಟ್ ಮತ್ತು ಮಾದರಿ ಆವೃತ್ತಿಗಳು ಎಲ್ಲವನ್ನೂ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಲೇಖಕ ಸ್ಕ್ರಿಪ್ಟ್‌ಗಳಾಗಿ ಬರೆದಿದ್ದಾರೆ, ಯಾವುದೇ ಮಾದರಿ ತರಬೇತಿ ಅಥವಾ ಪ್ರಶ್ನೆ ಇಲ್ಲ, ಸಾಧನಗಳು ಅನುಕರಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿವೆ ಮತ್ತು ಏನೂ ಕಾರ್ಯಗತವಾಗುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಮೂಲ code/main.py ಒದಗಿಸಿರಲಿಲ್ಲ ಮತ್ತು lesson ಕೋಡ್ ತುಣುಕುಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಮಾತ್ರ ತೋರಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿತು, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳು ನಮ್ಮದೇ ಅನುಷ್ಠಾನ ಮತ್ತು ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಅನ್ನು ಅವನ್ನು ಓಡಿಸಿ ಪಡೆಯಲಾಗಿದೆ. 2022 Constitutional AI ವಿಧಾನ, RLAIF, 2023 ಭಾಗವಹಿಕೆ ಪ್ರಯೋಗ ಮತ್ತು 2026 Claude Constitution ಬಗ್ಗೆ lesson ವಿವರಣೆ ಪರಿಕಲ್ಪನಾತ್ಮಕ ಅಥವಾ ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಿತ ಮತ್ತು ಇಲ್ಲಿ ಓಡಿಸಿಲ್ಲ ಅಥವಾ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಯಾವುದೇ ಮಾದರಿ ಇಲ್ಲ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Rules Cannot List Every Case, and Principles Cannot Be the Only Check","textKn":"ನಿಯಮಗಳು ಎಲ್ಲಾ ಪ್ರಕರಣ ಪಟ್ಟಿ ಮಾಡಲಾರವು, ತತ್ವಗಳೇ ಏಕೈಕ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ ಆಗಲಾರವು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Rules, Tiers, Allowlists and Labels","headingKn":"ನಿಯಮಗಳು, ಹಂತಗಳು, Allowlists ಮತ್ತು ಲೇಬಲ್‌ಗಳು","bodyEn":"This part first measures how an exact blocklist and a blanket delete rule do on a small labelled set, then builds the four-tier resolver the lesson describes: hard prohibitions are checked before anything else, each of the four tiers must have exactly one evaluation, the highest-priority block names the refusal and a modify decision returns an alternative. It then tests an operator allowlist against a naive dictionary merge and shows a category label supplied by the requester slipping past a check. The resolver combines evaluations it is given, and the lab writes those evaluations itself.","bodyKn":"ಈ ಭಾಗ ಮೊದಲು ಸಣ್ಣ ಲೇಬಲ್ ಮಾಡಿದ ಸೆಟ್‌ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಖರ blocklist ಮತ್ತು ಸಾರ್ವತ್ರಿಕ delete ನಿಯಮ ಹೇಗೆ ಕೆಲಸ ಮಾಡುತ್ತವೆ ಅಳೆಯುತ್ತದೆ, ನಂತರ lesson ವಿವರಿಸುವ ನಾಲ್ಕು-ಹಂತದ resolver ನಿರ್ಮಿಸುತ್ತದೆ: ಕಠಿಣ ನಿಷೇಧಗಳನ್ನು ಬೇರೆಲ್ಲದಕ್ಕಿಂತ ಮೊದಲು ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಲಾಗುತ್ತದೆ, ನಾಲ್ಕು ಹಂತಗಳಿಗೂ ಸರಿಯಾಗಿ ಒಂದು ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನ ಇರಬೇಕು, ಅತಿ ಹೆಚ್ಚಿನ ಆದ್ಯತೆಯ ತಡೆ ನಿರಾಕರಣೆಯನ್ನು ಹೆಸರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ ಮತ್ತು modify ನಿರ್ಧಾರ ಪರ್ಯಾಯ ಹಿಂತಿರುಗಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ನಂತರ ನೈವ್ ನಿಘಂಟು ವಿಲೀನದ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಆಪರೇಟರ್ allowlist ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಿ ವಿನಂತಿದಾರ ನೀಡಿದ ವರ್ಗ ಲೇಬಲ್ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ ದಾಟುವುದನ್ನು ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. resolver ತನಗೆ ನೀಡಿದ ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನಗಳನ್ನು ಸಂಯೋಜಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು ಆ ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನಗಳನ್ನು ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ತಾನೇ ಬರೆಯುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"Four Tiers and a Hard Floor","headingKn":"ನಾಲ್ಕು ಹಂತಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ಕಠಿಣ ತಳ","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">higher tiers win a genuine conflict</text><rect x="10" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="50" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">safety</text><text x="50" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">tier 1</text><rect x="110" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="150" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">ethics</text><text x="150" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">tier 2</text><rect x="210" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="250" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">guidelines</text><text x="250" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">tier 3</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="140" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">helpfulness</text><text x="150" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">tier 4, never above the rest</text><path d="M150,64 V110" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">higher tiers win a genuine conflict</text></svg>","captionEn":"Hard prohibitions are checked first, then tiers in priority order.","captionKn":"ಕಠಿಣ ನಿಷೇಧಗಳನ್ನು ಮೊದಲು ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಲಾಗುತ್ತದೆ, ನಂತರ ಆದ್ಯತೆ ಕ್ರಮದಲ್ಲಿ ಹಂತಗಳು."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"The resolver rules","headingKn":"resolver ನಿಯಮಗಳು","headers":["Step","What it does"],"rows":[["hard prohibition","checked first, refuses whatever the tiers say"],["evaluation count","exactly one per tier, otherwise an error"],["block","the highest-priority block names the refusal"],["modify","returns an alternative that still needs checking"],["allow","only when every tier passes"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building and Testing the Ideas","textKn":"ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"cn_1.py","headingEn":"Resolver, allowlist and rule baselines","headingKn":"Resolver, allowlist ಮತ್ತು ನಿಯಮ ಮೂಲರೇಖೆಗಳು","descEn":"resolve checks the hard prohibition, validates the four evaluations and returns the first block or modify in tier order, validate_operator_settings accepts only listed keys and values, and trusted_category re-derives a category from tags.","descKn":"resolve ಕಠಿಣ ನಿಷೇಧ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ ನಾಲ್ಕು ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನ ಮೌಲ್ಯೀಕರಿಸಿ ಹಂತ ಕ್ರಮದಲ್ಲಿ ಮೊದಲ block ಅಥವಾ modify ಹಿಂತಿರುಗಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, validate_operator_settings ಪಟ್ಟಿ ಮಾಡಿದ keys ಮತ್ತು ಮೌಲ್ಯಗಳನ್ನು ಮಾತ್ರ ಸ್ವೀಕರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು trusted_category tags ನಿಂದ ವರ್ಗ ಮರುಪಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"class Decision(str, Enum):
    ALLOW = "ALLOW"
    REFUSE = "REFUSE"
    MODIFY = "MODIFY"


class Evaluation(str, Enum):
    PASS = "PASS"
    BLOCK = "BLOCK"
    MODIFY = "MODIFY"


class Tier(Enum):
    SAFETY = 1
    ETHICS = 2
    GUIDELINES = 3
    HELPFULNESS = 4


HARD_PROHIBITIONS = frozenset({"prohibited_cbrn_assistance", "prohibited_child_exploitation", "prohibited_critical_infrastructure_attack"})


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class PrincipleEvaluation:
    tier: Tier
    result: Evaluation
    reason: str


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class ProposedAction:
    name: str
    description: str
    category: str
    evaluations: tuple
    alternative: str = ""


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class Resolution:
    decision: Decision
    reason: str
    controlling_tier: str
    alternative: str = ""


def checks(safety=Evaluation.PASS, ethics=Evaluation.PASS, guidelines=Evaluation.PASS, helpfulness=Evaluation.PASS):
    out = []
    for tier, res in ((Tier.SAFETY, safety), (Tier.ETHICS, ethics), (Tier.GUIDELINES, guidelines), (Tier.HELPFULNESS, helpfulness)):
        out.append(PrincipleEvaluation(tier, res, f"{tier.name} evaluation: {res.value}"))
    return tuple(out)


def resolve(action):
    if action.category in HARD_PROHIBITIONS:
        return Resolution(Decision.REFUSE, "Non-overridable prohibition", "HARD_PROHIBITION")
    tiers = [e.tier for e in action.evaluations]
    if len(tiers) != 4 or set(tiers) != set(Tier):
        raise ValueError("Exactly one evaluation per tier is required")
    ordered = sorted(action.evaluations, key=lambda e: e.tier.value)
    for item in ordered:
        if item.result == Evaluation.BLOCK:
            return Resolution(Decision.REFUSE, item.reason, item.tier.name)
    for item in ordered:
        if item.result == Evaluation.MODIFY:
            return Resolution(Decision.MODIFY, item.reason, item.tier.name, action.alternative)
    return Resolution(Decision.ALLOW, "All four evaluations passed", "NONE")


TRUSTED_TAGS = {"pathogen_synthesis_route": "prohibited_cbrn_assistance", "grid_control_takeover": "prohibited_critical_infrastructure_attack"}


def trusted_category(declared, tags):
    for t in tags:
        if t in TRUSTED_TAGS:
            return TRUSTED_TAGS[t]
    return declared


ALLOWED_SETTINGS = {"response_style": {"formal", "casual", "detailed"}, "response_length": {"short", "medium", "long"}}


def validate_operator_settings(settings):
    clean = {}
    for k, v in settings.items():
        if k not in ALLOWED_SETTINGS:
            raise ValueError(f"Unauthorized setting: {k}")
        if v not in ALLOWED_SETTINGS[k]:
            raise ValueError(f"Invalid value for {k}: {v}")
        clean[k] = v
    return clean


PROHIBITED_NAMES = {"delete_database", "disable_security", "expose_credentials"}


def exact_blocklist_allows(name):
    return name not in PROHIBITED_NAMES


def blanket_delete_allows(name):
    return "delete" not in name.lower()


# (name, truly acceptable, weakens oversight, destroys protected data, exposes a credential): attributes assigned by the lab author
LABELLED = [
    ("delete_database", False, False, True, False),
    ("remove_all_backup_snapshots", False, False, True, False),
    ("disable_audit_logs_for_speed", False, True, False, False),
    ("expose_api_key", False, False, False, True),
    ("export_signing_key", False, False, False, True),
    ("delete_obsolete_temp_file", True, False, False, False),
    ("delete_test_artifact_from_this_run", True, False, False, False),
    ("summarise_report", True, False, False, False),
    ("reduce_debug_logging", True, False, False, False),
    ("explain_python_dicts", True, False, False, False),
]


def principle_allows(row):
    return not (row[2] or row[3] or row[4])


class ResolverTests(unittest.TestCase):
    def mk(self, cat="education", **kw):
        return ProposedAction("a", "d", cat, checks(**kw), alternative="safer plan")

    def test_clear_allow(self):
        self.assertEqual(resolve(self.mk()).decision, Decision.ALLOW)

    def test_ethics_blocks_helpfulness(self):
        r = resolve(self.mk(ethics=Evaluation.BLOCK))
        self.assertEqual((r.decision, r.controlling_tier), (Decision.REFUSE, "ETHICS"))

    def test_hard_prohibition_beats_all_pass(self):
        self.assertEqual(resolve(self.mk(cat="prohibited_cbrn_assistance")).controlling_tier, "HARD_PROHIBITION")

    def test_safety_outranks_ethics(self):
        self.assertEqual(resolve(self.mk(safety=Evaluation.BLOCK, ethics=Evaluation.BLOCK)).controlling_tier, "SAFETY")

    def test_modify_carries_alternative(self):
        r = resolve(self.mk(safety=Evaluation.MODIFY))
        self.assertEqual((r.decision, r.alternative), (Decision.MODIFY, "safer plan"))

    def test_missing_evaluation_rejected(self):
        with self.assertRaises(ValueError):
            resolve(ProposedAction("a", "d", "x", checks()[:3]))"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"cn_1.py","headingEn":"main(): experiments","headingKn":"main(): ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"main() scores three rule styles, runs the resolver on six situations, tests the allowlist, shows a mislabelled category and runs six unit tests.","descKn":"main() ಮೂರು ನಿಯಮ ಶೈಲಿ ಅಂಕಿಸಿ, ಆರು ಸಂದರ್ಭಗಳ ಮೇಲೆ resolver ಓಡಿಸಿ, allowlist ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಿ, ತಪ್ಪು ಲೇಬಲ್ ವರ್ಗ ತೋರಿಸಿ ಮತ್ತು ಆರು unit ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆ ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def main():
    section("1. Genuinely running: enumerated rules against a labelled set")
    unsafe = [r for r in LABELLED if not r[1]]
    safe = [r for r in LABELLED if r[1]]
    for label, allows in (("exact blocklist", lambda r: exact_blocklist_allows(r[0])), ("blanket 'delete' rule", lambda r: blanket_delete_allows(r[0])), ("principle on attributes", principle_allows)):
        fa = [r[0] for r in unsafe if allows(r)]
        fr = [r[0] for r in safe if not allows(r)]
        print(f"{label:24} unsafe allowed {len(fa)} of {len(unsafe)} | acceptable refused {len(fr)} of {len(safe)}")
        if label != "principle on attributes":
            print(f"{'':24} missed: {fa}")
            if fr:
                print(f"{'':24} wrongly refused: {fr}")
    print("the exact blocklist let four of five unsafe actions through because it only knows three spellings, the blanket delete rule caught one and also refused two harmless cleanups, and the principle rule got every row right only because its attributes were filled in by the author who knew the answers, so it shows the shape of the approach and not an accuracy")

    section("2. Genuinely running: the four-tier resolver")
    cases = [
        ("Explain Python dictionaries", ProposedAction("c1", "d", "education", checks())),
        ("Create a misleading report", ProposedAction("c2", "d", "reporting", checks(ethics=Evaluation.BLOCK))),
        ("Prohibited action", ProposedAction("c3", "d", "prohibited_cbrn_assistance", checks())),
        ("Reduce production logging", ProposedAction("c4", "d", "operations", checks(safety=Evaluation.MODIFY), alternative="Reduce debug logging while preserving required audit records")),
    ]
    for title, a in cases:
        r = resolve(a)
        print(f"{title}: {r.decision.value} | controlling tier {r.controlling_tier} | reason: {r.reason}" + (f" | alternative: {r.alternative}" if r.alternative else ""))
    r = resolve(ProposedAction("c5", "d", "ops", checks(safety=Evaluation.BLOCK, ethics=Evaluation.BLOCK, helpfulness=Evaluation.PASS)))
    print("safety and ethics both block, helpfulness passes:", r.decision.value, "controlled by", r.controlling_tier)
    try:
        resolve(ProposedAction("c6", "d", "x", checks()[:3]))
    except ValueError as e:
        print("only three evaluations supplied:", e)
    print("a hard prohibition refuses even when all four tiers pass, the highest-priority block names the refusal, a modify decision returns an alternative that still has to be evaluated and authorised before anything runs, and an incomplete evaluation set is an error and not an approval; the resolver only combines evaluations it is given")

    section("3. Genuinely running: an operator allowlist against a dictionary merge")
    print("valid:", validate_operator_settings({"response_style": "formal", "response_length": "long"}))
    for bad in ({"disable_safety": "true"}, {"response_style": "sarcastic"}):
        try:
            validate_operator_settings(bad)
        except ValueError as e:
            print("rejected:", e)
    config = {"safety_checks": True, "response_style": "concise"}
    config.update({"response_style": "detailed", "safety_checks": False})
    print("naive config.update with an operator dictionary:", config)
    print("the allowlist accepted two known settings, refused an unknown key and an unknown value, and the naive merge let the operator switch safety_checks off; the allowlist protects the settings it lists and nothing else in the process")

    section("4. Genuinely running: a category label is not a security boundary")
