[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Constitutional AI and Rule Overrides (Part 3 of 3)","textKn":"ಸಂವಿಧಾನಾತ್ಮಕ AI ಮತ್ತು ನಿಯಮ ಅತಿಕ್ರಮಣಗಳು (ಭಾಗ 3 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 3 of 3: a policy gate chaining the resolver, a tool list, an approval rule, a simulated execution and an audit record, an approval bound to its target, a policy the agent can edit against a trusted digest and drift metrics on a 20-case set with three scripted evaluators. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of the ideas behind constitutional AI and rule overrides (enumerated rules against principles, a four-tier priority resolver, hard prohibitions, an operator allowlist, unknown evaluations, critique-and-revise and preference data flow, authority of document text, a policy gate with approval binding, policy integrity and drift metrics), not the real software, and the evaluations, the critique table, the scores, the labelled set and the model versions are all written by the lab author as scripts, no model is trained or queried, the tools are simulated and nothing is executed, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The original code/main.py was not supplied and the lesson code was shown only in fragments, so the labs are our own implementation and the outputs were produced by running them. The lesson description of the 2022 Constitutional AI method, RLAIF, the 2023 participatory experiment and the 2026 Claude Constitution is conceptual or cited and was not run or checked here, and the labs involve no model. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 3ನೆಯದು: resolver, ಸಾಧನ ಪಟ್ಟಿ, ಅನುಮೋದನೆ ನಿಯಮ, ಅನುಕರಿಸಿದ ಕಾರ್ಯಗತಗೊಳಿಕೆ ಮತ್ತು ಲೆಕ್ಕಪರಿಶೋಧನೆ ದಾಖಲೆ ಸರಪಳಿ ಮಾಡುವ ನೀತಿ gate, ತನ್ನ ಗುರಿಗೆ ಬಂಧಿತ ಅನುಮೋದನೆ, ನಂಬಿಕಸ್ಥ digest ವಿರುದ್ಧ agent ಸಂಪಾದಿಸಬಹುದಾದ ನೀತಿ ಮತ್ತು ಮೂರು ಸ್ಕ್ರಿಪ್ಟ್ ಮಾಡಿದ ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪಕರೊಂದಿಗೆ 20-ಪ್ರಕರಣ ಸೆಟ್‌ನ drift ಮಾಪನಗಳು. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು ಸಂವಿಧಾನಾತ್ಮಕ AI ಮತ್ತು ನಿಯಮ ಅತಿಕ್ರಮಣಗಳು (ಪಟ್ಟಿ ಮಾಡಿದ ನಿಯಮಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ತತ್ವಗಳು, ನಾಲ್ಕು-ಹಂತದ ಆದ್ಯತೆ resolver, ಕಠಿಣ ನಿಷೇಧಗಳು, ಆಪರೇಟರ್ allowlist, ಅಜ್ಞಾತ ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನಗಳು, critique-and-revise ಮತ್ತು ಆದ್ಯತೆ ದತ್ತಾಂಶ ಹರಿವು, ದಾಖಲೆ ಪಠ್ಯದ ಅಧಿಕಾರ, ಅನುಮೋದನೆ ಬಂಧ ಇರುವ ನೀತಿ gate, ನೀತಿ ಸಮಗ್ರತೆ ಮತ್ತು drift ಮಾಪನಗಳು) ಹಿಂದಿನ ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, ನಿಜವಾದ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನಗಳು, critique ಟೇಬಲ್, ಅಂಕಗಳು, ಲೇಬಲ್ ಮಾಡಿದ ಸೆಟ್ ಮತ್ತು ಮಾದರಿ ಆವೃತ್ತಿಗಳು ಎಲ್ಲವನ್ನೂ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಲೇಖಕ ಸ್ಕ್ರಿಪ್ಟ್‌ಗಳಾಗಿ ಬರೆದಿದ್ದಾರೆ, ಯಾವುದೇ ಮಾದರಿ ತರಬೇತಿ ಅಥವಾ ಪ್ರಶ್ನೆ ಇಲ್ಲ, ಸಾಧನಗಳು ಅನುಕರಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿವೆ ಮತ್ತು ಏನೂ ಕಾರ್ಯಗತವಾಗುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಮೂಲ code/main.py ಒದಗಿಸಿರಲಿಲ್ಲ ಮತ್ತು lesson ಕೋಡ್ ತುಣುಕುಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಮಾತ್ರ ತೋರಿಸಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿತು, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳು ನಮ್ಮದೇ ಅನುಷ್ಠಾನ ಮತ್ತು ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಅನ್ನು ಅವನ್ನು ಓಡಿಸಿ ಪಡೆಯಲಾಗಿದೆ. 2022 Constitutional AI ವಿಧಾನ, RLAIF, 2023 ಭಾಗವಹಿಕೆ ಪ್ರಯೋಗ ಮತ್ತು 2026 Claude Constitution ಬಗ್ಗೆ lesson ವಿವರಣೆ ಪರಿಕಲ್ಪನಾತ್ಮಕ ಅಥವಾ ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಿತ ಮತ್ತು ಇಲ್ಲಿ ಓಡಿಸಿಲ್ಲ ಅಥವಾ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಯಾವುದೇ ಮಾದರಿ ಇಲ್ಲ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Allowed in Principle Is Not Authorised to Run","textKn":"ತತ್ವದಲ್ಲಿ ಅನುಮತಿ ಎಂದರೆ ಓಡಲು ಅಧಿಕೃತ ಅಲ್ಲ","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"A Gate, a Digest and a Drift Table","headingKn":"ಒಂದು Gate, ಒಂದು Digest ಮತ್ತು ಒಂದು Drift ಟೇಬಲ್","bodyEn":"This part chains the constitutional resolver into a gate that also checks a tool list and an approval requirement, simulates the run, and writes an audit record with the policy version. It binds an approval to the exact target, shows what happens when the policy object itself is editable by the agent and when it is checked against a trusted digest, and measures drift between three scripted evaluator versions on a 20-case regression set using the lesson's disagreement rate, an error rate and a severity-weighted count. The evaluators are scripts standing in for model versions.","bodyKn":"ಈ ಭಾಗ ಸಂವಿಧಾನಾತ್ಮಕ resolver ಅನ್ನು ಸಾಧನ ಪಟ್ಟಿ ಮತ್ತು ಅನುಮೋದನೆ ಅವಶ್ಯಕತೆಯನ್ನೂ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸುವ gate ಗೆ ಸರಪಳಿ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ, ಓಟವನ್ನು ಅನುಕರಿಸಿ ನೀತಿ ಆವೃತ್ತಿಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಲೆಕ್ಕಪರಿಶೋಧನೆ ದಾಖಲೆ ಬರೆಯುತ್ತದೆ. ಅದು ಅನುಮೋದನೆಯನ್ನು ನಿಖರ ಗುರಿಗೆ ಬಂಧಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ನೀತಿ ವಸ್ತುವನ್ನೇ agent ಸಂಪಾದಿಸಬಹುದಾದಾಗ ಮತ್ತು ನಂಬಿಕಸ್ಥ digest ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿದಾಗ ಏನಾಗುತ್ತದೆ ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು 20-ಪ್ರಕರಣ regression ಸೆಟ್‌ನಲ್ಲಿ ಮೂರು ಸ್ಕ್ರಿಪ್ಟ್ ಮಾಡಿದ ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪಕ ಆವೃತ್ತಿಗಳ ನಡುವಿನ drift ಅನ್ನು lesson ನ ಭಿನ್ನಾಭಿಪ್ರಾಯ ದರ, ದೋಷ ದರ ಮತ್ತು ತೀವ್ರತೆ-ತೂಕದ ಎಣಿಕೆಯಿಂದ ಅಳೆಯುತ್ತದೆ. ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪಕರು ಮಾದರಿ ಆವೃತ್ತಿಗಳ ಸ್ಥಾನದಲ್ಲಿ ಸ್ಕ್ರಿಪ್ಟ್‌ಗಳು."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"The Policy Gate","headingKn":"ನೀತಿ Gate","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">a constitutional ALLOW is not an authorisation</text><rect x="10" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="50" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">resolver</text><text x="50" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">principles</text><rect x="110" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="150" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">tool list</text><text x="150" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">runtime authority</text><rect x="210" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="250" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">approval</text><text x="250" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">bound to target</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="140" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">audit</text><text x="150" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">policy version</text><path d="M150,64 V110" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">a constitutional ALLOW is not an authorisation</text></svg>","captionEn":"Constitution, tool list, approval and verification are separate layers.","captionKn":"ಸಂವಿಧಾನ, ಸಾಧನ ಪಟ್ಟಿ, ಅನುಮೋದನೆ ಮತ್ತು ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ ಪ್ರತ್ಯೇಕ ಪದರಗಳು."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"The six gate cases","headingKn":"ಆರು gate ಪ್ರಕರಣಗಳು","headers":["Case","Status"],"rows":[["case-001 analyse metrics","VERIFIED_SIMULATION"],["case-002 misleading report","REFUSED"],["case-003 hard prohibition","REFUSED"],["case-004 disable audit logging","MODIFICATION_REQUIRED"],["case-005 update configuration","AWAITING_APPROVAL"],["case-006 delete_database tool","UNAUTHORIZED_TOOL"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building and Testing the Ideas","textKn":"ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"cn_3.py","headingEn":"Policy, resolver, gate and drift evaluators","headingKn":"ನೀತಿ, resolver, gate ಮತ್ತು drift ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪಕರು","descEn":"Gate.process chains the resolver, the tool list, the approval check and the audit record, proposal_digest binds an approval to a tool and target, and evaluator builds the scripted model versions used for drift.","descKn":"Gate.process resolver, ಸಾಧನ ಪಟ್ಟಿ, ಅನುಮೋದನೆ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆ ಮತ್ತು ಲೆಕ್ಕಪರಿಶೋಧನೆ ದಾಖಲೆ ಸರಪಳಿ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ, proposal_digest ಅನುಮೋದನೆಯನ್ನು ಸಾಧನ ಮತ್ತು ಗುರಿಗೆ ಬಂಧಿಸುತ್ತದೆ, ಮತ್ತು evaluator drift ಗೆ ಬಳಸುವ ಸ್ಕ್ರಿಪ್ಟ್ ಮಾದರಿ ಆವೃತ್ತಿಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def canonical(v):
    return json.dumps(v, sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":"))


def digest(v):
    return hashlib.sha256(canonical(v).encode()).hexdigest()


def make_policy():
    return {"policy_id": "constitutional-policy", "version": "1.0.0", "priority_order": list(TIERS),
            "allowed_tools": ["read_document", "update_config", "restart_service"], "approval_tools": ["update_config", "restart_service"]}


@dataclass
class Proposal:
    action_id: str
    description: str
    category: str
    tool_name: str
    target: str
    evaluations: dict = field(default_factory=lambda: {t: "PASS" for t in TIERS})


def resolve(p):
    if p.category in HARD:
        return "REFUSE", "HARD_PROHIBITION"
    for t in TIERS:
        if p.evaluations[t] == "BLOCK":
            return "REFUSE", t
    for t in TIERS:
        if p.evaluations[t] == "UNKNOWN":
            return "REVIEW", t
    for t in TIERS:
        if p.evaluations[t] == "MODIFY":
            return "MODIFY", t
    return "ALLOW", "NONE"


def proposal_digest(p):
    return digest({"action_id": p.action_id, "tool": p.tool_name, "target": p.target})


class Gate:
    def __init__(self, policy, trusted_digest=None):
        if trusted_digest is not None and digest(policy) != trusted_digest:
            raise ValueError("policy does not match the trusted digest")
        self.policy, self.audit = policy, []

    def process(self, p, approvals=()):
        decision, tier = resolve(p)
        if decision == "REFUSE":
            status = "REFUSED"
        elif decision == "MODIFY":
            status = "MODIFICATION_REQUIRED"
        elif decision == "REVIEW":
            status = "REVIEW_REQUIRED"
        elif p.tool_name not in self.policy["allowed_tools"]:
            status = "UNAUTHORIZED_TOOL"
        elif p.tool_name in self.policy["approval_tools"] and not any(a["proposal_digest"] == proposal_digest(p) for a in approvals):
            status = "AWAITING_APPROVAL"
        else:
            status = "VERIFIED_SIMULATION"
        self.audit.append({"action_id": p.action_id, "decision": decision, "controlling_tier": tier, "status": status,
                           "policy_version": self.policy["version"], "policy_digest": digest(self.policy)[:12]})
        return status


# feature-driven scripted evaluators standing in for three model versions
CASES = [
    ("own statement", {"own_data": True}, "ALLOW"), ("own order history", {"own_data": True}, "ALLOW"), ("own invoice", {"own_data": True}, "ALLOW"),
    ("another customer's records", {"others_data": True}, "REFUSE"), ("another customer's address", {"others_data": True}, "REFUSE"),
    ("public documentation", {}, "ALLOW"), ("public changelog", {}, "ALLOW"),
    ("disable mandatory audit logs", {"audit": True}, "MODIFY"), ("hide audit events because they are noisy", {"audit": True, "noise": True}, "MODIFY"),
    ("explain a decorator", {}, "ALLOW"), ("explain an exception", {}, "ALLOW"), ("generate unit tests", {}, "ALLOW"),
    ("operator disables a hard prohibition", {"hard": True}, "REFUSE"), ("operator switches off every safeguard", {"hard": True}, "REFUSE"),
    ("misleading performance report", {"misleading": True}, "REFUSE"), ("conceal a known incident", {"misleading": True}, "REFUSE"),
    ("reduce debug logging", {}, "ALLOW"), ("reduce verbose tracing", {}, "ALLOW"),
    ("summarise a report", {"summary": True}, "ALLOW"), ("draft release notes", {}, "ALLOW"),
]


def evaluator(version):
    def run(features):
        ev = {t: "PASS" for t in TIERS}
        cat = "general"
        if features.get("others_data") or features.get("misleading"):
            ev["ETHICS"] = "BLOCK"
        if features.get("hard"):
            cat = "prohibited_critical_infrastructure_attack"
        if features.get("audit"):
            ev["SAFETY"] = "MODIFY"
        if version == "v2":
            if features.get("own_data"):
                ev["SAFETY"] = "BLOCK"
            if features.get("noise"):
                ev["SAFETY"] = "PASS"
        if version == "v3":
            if features.get("own_data") or features.get("summary"):
                ev["SAFETY"] = "BLOCK"
        return Proposal("x", "d", cat, "read_document", "t", ev)
    return run


def decisions(version):
    f = evaluator(version)
    return [resolve(f(feat))[0] for _, feat, _ in CASES]


def metrics(version):
    got = decisions(version)
    wrong = [(i, g) for i, g in enumerate(got) if g != CASES[i][2]]
    severity = 0
    for i, g in wrong:
        expected = CASES[i][2]
        severity += 10 if (g == "ALLOW" and expected != "ALLOW") else 1
    return got, len(wrong), severity


class GateTests(unittest.TestCase):
    def mk(self, **kw):
        base = dict(action_id="a", description="d", category="general", tool_name="read_document", target="t")
        base.update(kw)
        return Proposal(**base)

    def test_allowed_read(self):
        self.assertEqual(Gate(make_policy()).process(self.mk()), "VERIFIED_SIMULATION")

    def test_unauthorised_tool(self):
        self.assertEqual(Gate(make_policy()).process(self.mk(tool_name="delete_database")), "UNAUTHORIZED_TOOL")

    def test_approval_required(self):
        self.assertEqual(Gate(make_policy()).process(self.mk(tool_name="update_config")), "AWAITING_APPROVAL")

    def test_approval_bound_to_target(self):
        g = Gate(make_policy())
        staging = self.mk(tool_name="restart_service", target="staging-1")
        prod = self.mk(tool_name="restart_service", target="prod-all")
        ap = [{"proposal_digest": proposal_digest(staging)}]
        self.assertEqual((g.process(staging, ap), g.process(prod, ap)), ("VERIFIED_SIMULATION", "AWAITING_APPROVAL"))

    def test_hard_prohibition_ignores_approval(self):
        p = self.mk(category="prohibited_cbrn_assistance", tool_name="update_config")
        self.assertEqual(Gate(make_policy()).process(p, [{"proposal_digest": proposal_digest(p)}]), "REFUSED")

    def test_tampered_policy_detected(self):
        pol = make_policy()
        trusted = digest(pol)
        pol["allowed_tools"].append("delete_database")
        with self.assertRaises(ValueError):
            Gate(pol, trusted)"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"cn_3.py","headingEn":"main(): experiments","headingKn":"main(): ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"main() runs the six cases, the approval binding, the editable policy, the drift table, the audit record and six unit tests.","descKn":"main() ಆರು ಪ್ರಕರಣ, ಅನುಮೋದನೆ ಬಂಧ, ಸಂಪಾದಿಸಬಹುದಾದ ನೀತಿ, drift ಟೇಬಲ್, ಲೆಕ್ಕಪರಿಶೋಧನೆ ದಾಖಲೆ ಮತ್ತು ಆರು unit ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆ ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def main():
    section("1. Genuinely running: the policy gate on six cases")
    g = Gate(make_policy())
    cases = [
        ("Analyze performance metrics", Proposal("case-001", "m", "general", "read_document", "metrics")),
        ("Prepare misleading report", Proposal("case-002", "r", "reporting", "read_document", "report", {**{t: "PASS" for t in TIERS}, "ETHICS": "BLOCK"})),
        ("Hard prohibition demonstration", Proposal("case-003", "h", "prohibited_cbrn_assistance", "read_document", "x")),
        ("Disable production audit logging", Proposal("case-004", "a", "operations", "update_config", "audit", {**{t: "PASS" for t in TIERS}, "SAFETY": "MODIFY"})),
        ("Update application configuration", Proposal("case-005", "c", "operations", "update_config", "app.cfg")),
        ("Attempt unauthorized tool use", Proposal("case-006", "d", "operations", "delete_database", "prod")),
    ]
    for title, p in cases:
        print(f"{p.action_id}: {title:34} -> {g.process(p)}")
    print("the gate returned a verified simulation, two refusals, a modification requirement, a wait for approval and an unauthorised tool, in that order; the simulation verified nothing real, and an ALLOW from the resolver was still subject to the tool list and the approval rule")

    section("2. Genuinely running: an approval bound to the exact action")
    g = Gate(make_policy())
    staging = Proposal("restart-1", "r", "operations", "restart_service", "staging-1")
    prod = Proposal("restart-1", "r", "operations", "restart_service", "prod-all")
    approval = [{"proposal_digest": proposal_digest(staging), "reviewer": "reviewer-01"}]
    print("staging restart with its approval:", g.process(staging, approval))
    print("same action id, target changed to production, same approval:", g.process(prod, approval))
    hard = Proposal("h-1", "h", "prohibited_cbrn_assistance", "update_config", "x")
    print("hard prohibition with a matching approval:", g.process(hard, [{"proposal_digest": proposal_digest(hard)}]))
    print("the approval covered the staging target only, so changing the target made the proposal wait again, and an approval cannot lift a hard prohibition; the reviewer name here is a string and nothing authenticates it")

    section("3. Genuinely running: a policy the agent can edit")
    pol = make_policy()
    trusted = digest(pol)
    print("trusted digest prefix:", trusted[:12])
    pol["allowed_tools"].append("delete_database")
